  "as_of": "2023-05-25",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would clarify which child care subsidy overpayment debts belong to providers and which remain the responsibility of families receiving the payments.",
   "Providers would generally owe debts from incorrect attendance claims, but families would retain responsibility for withheld amounts subsequently paid directly to them after reconciliation.",
   "The changes would start the day after Royal Assent and apply to care sessions occurring from commencement, covering Child Care Subsidy and Additional Child Care Subsidy."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Providers would owe subsidy debts for ineligible absences before a child's first physical attendance.",
   "The same provider liability would cover ineligible absences after a child's last physical attendance.",
   "Provider-fault debt calculations would exclude withholding components paid to individuals.",
   "Rules would prevent charging providers twice for the same care session under overlapping debt provisions."
  ],
  "affected": "Approved child care providers, subsidy recipients and families whose children have attendance changes are affected.",
